        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Players try to collect four equal cards so they can show them and exit the game; the last two players remaining are the losers, and whoever holds the Joker cannot exit.',
          gameplay: '1. All players discard matching pairs (e.g., two Queens, two 7s).\n2. Each player in turn draws one card from the person to their right.\n3. If it matches a card in hand, discard the pair. If not, add it to your hand.\n4. **EXIT**: If you have NO cards left and do NOT hold the Joker, you are safe and leave the game.\n5. **The Joker Rule**: You can NEVER exit if you have the Joker. You must wait for someone to draw it from you.',
          keyRules: [
            'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Jukha.',
            'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Scoring follows the game-specific point or pot rules.',
            'Winning condition: Avoid being the last player holding the Joker.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep your cards close but the Joker accessible. If you show a 'tell' that a card is the Joker (like a slight flinch or a smirk), you'll never get rid of it.",
          intermediate: "The 'Lure': When someone draws from you, push your most useless non-matching card forward. If they take it, they haven't won anything. If they hesitate, they might suspect it's the Joker and pick a different cardâ€”which IS the Joker.",
          advanced: "Card Tracking: With fewer players, remember which ranks have already been paired and discarded. This tells you which cards in your hand are 'guaranteed pairs' (cards that haven't appeared in the discard pile yet).",
          tips: [
            "The Joker is the 'Jukha'. If you have it, don't panic. Just keep passing!",
            'If you have only two cards left and one is the Joker, you need to be extremely convincing to get someone to take it.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
